# What Git must never carry to GitHub.
#
# Nothing here is deleted from your computer - .gitignore only decides what
# gets committed. Your .env and your SQLite database stay exactly where they
# are; they simply never leave the machine.

# --- SECRETS -----------------------------------------------------------
# The single most important block in this file. .env holds SECRET_KEY and,
# in other setups, database passwords. Committing it - even to a private
# repository - is how real credential leaks happen.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- LOCAL DATABASE ----------------------------------------------------
# Your development database and every backup beside it. This is test data,
# it belongs on your laptop, and production starts from an empty PostgreSQL
# database instead.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
instance/
backend/instance/

# --- PYTHON ------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- NODE --------------------------------------------------------------
# Thousands of downloaded files, rebuilt from package-lock.json with
# `npm install`. Never commit them.
node_modules/

# --- BUILD OUTPUT ------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE the deliberate exception below.
#
# frontend/dist IS committed. Normally a build artifact does not belong in
# version control - but AWS builds this project FROM GitHub, and the Python
# runtime there has no Node.js, so it cannot run `vite build` itself. If the
# built files were not in the repository, the deployed site would have a
# working API and no user interface at all.
#
# The trade-off: you must rebuild the frontend and commit it whenever you
# change anything under frontend/src.
#
# (The cleaner alternative is a multi-stage Docker build that compiles the
# frontend on AWS. That removes this exception at the cost of learning
# Docker - a fair trade later, unnecessary complexity now.)
dist-ssr/
build/
.vite/
*.local

# --- LOGS --------------------------------------------------------------
*.log

# --- EDITORS / OS ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
